.TH APPROX 1 approx\-VERSION
.SH NAME
approx \- non-interactive fuzzy stream filter and ranker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B approx
.RB [ \-cCDehHilLmqsvV ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR threshold ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR count ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR max ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR delim ]
.RB [ \-k
.IR field ]
.RB [ \-F
.IR file ]
.RI [ pattern ]
.RI [ file\ ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B approx
filters and ranks text lines by comparing them against a search
.I pattern
(or a list of patterns from a file) using approximate string matching.
.P
If no
.I file
operands are specified, or if a file operand is
.BR \- ,
.B approx
reads from standard input.
.P
If two or more
.I file
operands are specified,
.B approx
automatically prefixes matching lines with their corresponding filename (grep-compatible behavior).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c
Output only the count of matching lines.
.TP
.B \-C
Highlight the matched substring using ANSI escape sequences.
.TP
.BI \-d " delim"
Set the field delimiter character for
.BR \-k .
Default is whitespace.
.TP
.B \-D
Enable Damerau-Levenshtein distance to count adjacent character transpositions as 1 edit.
.TP
.B \-e
Compare full lines instead of finding the best matching substring.
.TP
.BI \-F " file"
Read search patterns from
.IR file ,
one per line.
.TP
.B \-h
Never print filename prefixes in output (suppress filename prefix, not help).
.TP
.B \-H
Print the filename prefix for each match. Default when two or more file operands are specified.
.TP
.B \-i
Match case-insensitively.
.TP
.BI \-k " field"
Compare similarity against 1-based field number
.I field
while printing the full line.
.TP
.B \-l
Print only names of files with matching lines.
.TP
.B \-L
Print only names of files without matching lines.
.TP
.BI \-m " max"
Stop reading after finding
.I max
matching lines.
.TP
.BI \-n " count"
Output only the top
.I count
lines sorted by highest similarity score.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode. Suppress standard output and exit immediately on the first match.
.TP
.B \-s
Prepend the similarity score and a tab character before each matching line.
.TP
.BI \-t " threshold"
Minimum similarity score between
.B 0.00
and
.B 1.00
for a line to match. Default is
.BR 0.70 .
.TP
.B \-v
Invert match, selecting lines with scores below the threshold.
.TP
.B \-V
Print version information to standard output and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
At least one matching line was selected.
.TP
.B 1
No lines were selected.
.TP
.B >1
An error occurred.
.SH EXAMPLES
Filter log lines for typos in "connection timeout":
.IP
.EX
cat server.log | approx "connection timeout"
.EE
.P
Search column 2 of a CSV file for typoed names:
.IP
.EX
approx -d, -k 2 "john_doe" users.csv
.EE
.P
Tolerate swapped letters with Damerau-Levenshtein:
.IP
.EX
approx -D -t 0.85 "receive" /usr/share/dict/words
.EE
.P
Check condition in shell scripts quietly:
.IP
.EX
if approx -q "FATAL" /var/log/app.log; then echo "error found"; fi
.EE
.P
Find the top 5 closest matches with scores:
.IP
.EX
approx -n 5 -s "recieve" /usr/share/dict/words
.EE
